WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.679 --> 00:00:04.664
Eh, imagine this. Got a sensor in the river, every hour

2
00:00:04.684 --> 00:00:06.504
it save 1 water level.

3
00:00:06.524 --> 00:00:11.517
After 5 hours you got 5 numbers: minus 4, 12, 7,

4
00:00:11.537 --> 00:00:13.134
minus 9, 15.

5
00:00:13.164 --> 00:00:15.224
Then people ask you 3 things.

6
00:00:15.244 --> 00:00:16.424
What is the total?

7
00:00:16.444 --> 00:00:18.024
How many above 10?

8
00:00:18.044 --> 00:00:19.302
Which one the highest?

9
00:00:19.924 --> 00:00:22.144
Sounds like 3 different problems, right?

10
00:00:22.164 --> 00:00:25.094
Where got! Actually all the SAME pattern.

11
00:00:25.591 --> 00:00:27.304
Today we do 2 things lah.

12
00:00:27.324 --> 00:00:30.064
First, the 3 ways to walk through a list.

13
00:00:30.084 --> 00:00:35.064
Second, the accumulator pattern: sum, count, max, and filter into a

14
00:00:35.084 --> 00:00:35.974
new list.

15
00:00:36.124 --> 00:00:39.264
Learn this pattern properly, a lot of loop questions in the

16
00:00:39.284 --> 00:00:41.014
exam settle already.

17
00:00:42.999 --> 00:00:45.059
The list we call levels.

18
00:00:45.079 --> 00:00:47.859
Way 1: for level in levels.

19
00:00:47.879 --> 00:00:52.939
Each round, level is the ITEM itself: minus 4, then 12,

20
00:00:52.959 --> 00:00:56.569
then 7. Use this when you only need the values.

21
00:00:56.603 --> 00:01:00.303
Way 2: for i in range len levels.

22
00:01:00.323 --> 00:01:05.183
Now i is the POSITION: 0, 1, 2, 3, 4.

23
00:01:05.203 --> 00:01:09.663
Stop value 5 not included, so exactly the valid indexes.

24
00:01:09.683 --> 00:01:11.943
The item is levels at i.

25
00:01:11.963 --> 00:01:14.623
Use this when you must know WHERE, or when you want

26
00:01:14.643 --> 00:01:16.303
to change the list.

27
00:01:16.323 --> 00:01:20.423
Way 3: for i, level in enumerate levels.

28
00:01:20.443 --> 00:01:24.343
This one give you both together, position first, then item.

29
00:01:24.363 --> 00:01:26.664
Shiok. Why need the position ah?

30
00:01:26.684 --> 00:01:30.824
Because level equals 0 only change the name level, the list

31
00:01:30.844 --> 00:01:34.774
never change. Must write levels at i equals 0.

32
00:01:34.994 --> 00:01:37.585
The trap: dun mix the styles.

33
00:01:37.605 --> 00:01:40.745
In way 1, level is already the item.

34
00:01:40.765 --> 00:01:44.345
You write levels at level, now Python use minus 4 as

35
00:01:44.365 --> 00:01:46.855
an INDEX. Nonsense already!

36
00:01:49.052 --> 00:01:51.610
Now the pattern. Always 3 steps.

37
00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:55.280
Step 1, BEFORE the loop: give a start value.

38
00:01:55.310 --> 00:01:58.450
Step 2, INSIDE the loop: update.

39
00:01:58.470 --> 00:02:01.760
Step 3, AFTER the loop: use the answer.

40
00:02:01.794 --> 00:02:06.614
Sum: total equals 0, then total plus equals level.

41
00:02:06.634 --> 00:02:11.414
End with 21. Count: count equals 0, and if level more

42
00:02:11.434 --> 00:02:14.134
than 10, count plus equals 1.

43
00:02:14.154 --> 00:02:18.254
End with 2. Filter: start with an EMPTY list, and if

44
00:02:18.274 --> 00:02:20.414
level more than 10, append it.

45
00:02:20.434 --> 00:02:22.374
You get 12 and 15.

46
00:02:22.394 --> 00:02:23.936
Same 3 steps, see?

47
00:02:23.956 --> 00:02:26.496
Then max, the highest so far.

48
00:02:26.516 --> 00:02:27.886
What is the start value?

49
00:02:29.557 --> 00:02:31.577
Many people write 0.

50
00:02:31.597 --> 00:02:32.367
Aiyo.

51
00:02:32.677 --> 00:02:36.777
Take the levels minus 4, minus 9, minus 2.

52
00:02:36.797 --> 00:02:40.657
Nobody beat 0, so the answer is 0, but the sensor

53
00:02:40.677 --> 00:02:42.287
NEVER measure 0!

54
00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:47.097
So start with the first item: highest equals levels at 0.

55
00:02:47.117 --> 00:02:51.057
Why ah? Because the first item confirm inside the list.

56
00:02:51.077 --> 00:02:55.777
Another trap: start value INSIDE the loop will reset every round,

57
00:02:55.797 --> 00:02:57.777
so keep it before the loop.

58
00:02:57.797 --> 00:02:59.497
And return inside the loop?

59
00:02:59.517 --> 00:03:01.777
The function stop at the first item.

60
00:03:01.797 --> 00:03:03.727
The answer come AFTER.

61
00:03:05.734 --> 00:03:11.464
The one-line takeaway: start BEFORE, update inside, answer after.

62
00:03:11.494 --> 00:03:14.914
Sum and count start at 0, max start at the first

63
00:03:14.934 --> 00:03:18.184
item, filter start with an empty list.

64
00:03:18.218 --> 00:03:22.508
The practice notebook got 6 exercises with the same river sensor.

65
00:03:22.538 --> 00:03:25.878
2 to predict, 2 fix the bug, then 2 you write

66
00:03:25.898 --> 00:03:29.638
from scratch: keep only the calm levels, and find the first

67
00:03:29.658 --> 00:03:31.242
hour the river flood.

68
00:03:31.262 --> 00:03:34.842
And hor, graded work must be your OWN, the course does

69
00:03:34.862 --> 00:03:36.482
not allow AI on it.

70
00:03:36.502 --> 00:03:39.882
Practise here until steady, then that one you do yourself.

71
00:03:39.902 --> 00:03:41.672
Can one lah. Jia you!
